    "body": "## Problem\r\n`:detach!` changes the channel's detach property without emitting `ChanInfo`, so plugins watching channel updates cannot react to changes.\r\n\r\nBesides `:detach!`, these emit `ChanInfo`:\r\n1. `nvim_chan_set(chan, { detach = true/false })` — either value, even if it hasn’t changed.\r\n2. `nvim_set_client_info(...)` — updates the client’s name, version, type, methods, or attributes.\r\n\r\nSo for consistency it would make sense to add one for `:detach!`\r\n\r\n## Solution\r\nSchedule `ChanInfo` after setting `detach=true`. Add a test covering channel property updates, client metadata updates, and `:detach!`.\r\n\r\nNote: Used AI to assist (wrote test). Reviewed code and tested manually.",
    "closed_at": null,
    "comment_data": [],
    "comment_regular_data": [
        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "A small note for the future:\r\n\r\nIt's more important that _you_ communicate with _us_ than clarify that AI helped. For example, AI can write all of the code - but what's _more_ important is that you explain the change yourself intuitively (which you didn't). It doesn't really matter here, since it's a small change, but the extra effort does go a long way.\r\n\r\nYou taking responsibility for the code (\"Reviewed code and tested manually\") is the expectation.\r\n\r\nIs there a reason AI-assisted is not in the commit body (genuine question)? Is that removed now?",
